.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DEFERRED_PROBE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_defer_probe ,
.Nm device_retry_deferred
.Nd queue and retry deferred device probes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft void
.Fn device_defer_probe "struct device *dev"
.Ft void
.Fn device_retry_deferred void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_defer_probe
function adds a device to the global deferred-probe queue if it is not already
queued.
.Pp
The queue holds a reference on each deferred device so that retry processing
can safely run after the original probe site has returned.
.Pp
The
.Fn device_retry_deferred
function drains the deferred-probe queue and calls
.Xr device_probe 9
for each queued device.
If a retry again returns
.Dv -EDEFER ,
the device is requeued.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device_probe 9 ,
.Xr driver_register 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
interfaces first appeared in Substrate.
